    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0761" n="659" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg659"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.003/564: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-06T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1919,
                                noon.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your May 28, 8 p.m.</p>
                <p>Draft of Revised Import Tariff received with Arnold’s letter of December 18,
                        1918,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d650-f1"/> had three rules on page numbered 39
                    pasted to draft, and sheet of additions and corrections pasted on inside front
                    cover. No rules or additions and corrections with copies of Tariff received with
                    Arnold’s letter April 3. Advise whether those sent with letter December 18 were
                    final and whether they and the Draft of Tariff were agreed to by delegates of
                    foreign nations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d650-f1" n="83" xml:id="d650-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; for the rules in question, see <ref target="#pg663">pp.
